**Ideas & Value Propositions**
1. AI Academic Navigator
To build a personalized AI assistant web application that connects a student to the college's academic and networking information.
Why it's valuable: Students often struggle not because information doesn't exist, but because the information is scattered across dozens of systems and websites.
--> Value Proposition: "Navigate your degree, not the bureaucracy." This personalized AI assistant transforms scattered institutional data into a single, intuitive web application. By instantly connecting students to their specific academic requirements, advisor schedules, and campus resources, the app eliminates administrative friction—freeing them to focus entirely on their craft, studio time, networking and career preparation

2. AI Assignment Planner
To build an AI web application that helps students break large assignments and projects into manageable steps, instead of doing assignments for students.
It could also integrate with the student's calendar.
This would be especially useful for students taking multiple classes simultaneously.
--> Value Proposition: "Deconstruct the brief. Master the process." This AI-driven web application transforms overwhelming, open-ended assignments into clear, actionable workflows. By acting as a strategic planning partner rather than an automatic generator, it empowers students to organize their time, overcome blank-page paralysis, and build the critical project management skills essential for the professional creative industry.

3. AI Professor/Assignment FAQ
To build an AI web application that is trained in the professor's approved course information.
Students get immediate answers while professors spend less time responding to repetitive emails.
The professor could also see:
Top questions students asked this week
That could reveal where assignment instructions are unclear.
--> Value Proposition: Instant student support. Effortless instructor insights. This AI web application acts as a secure, dual-purpose academic tool. By training exclusively on a professor’s verified materials, it provides students with immediate, accurate academic support while transforming student inquiries into actionable data to improve course design.
